123 - As With Gladness Men of Old
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 123
Topic: Jesus Christ - 

Verse 1:
[G]As with gladness men [C/G]of old
[C/G]Did the [G]guiding star behold,
[Em]As with joy [Am/E]they [Em]hailed [Cm/D#]its light,
[C]Leadingonward, [D]beaming [G]bright,
[Bm/F#]So, most [Em]gracious [C]Lord, [D7]may [G]we
[C]Ever [G/B]more [Am]beled [D7]to Thee.

Verse 2:
[G]As with joyful steps [C/G]they sped
[C/G]To that [G]lowly manger bed,
[Em]There to bend [Am/E]the [Em]knee [Cm/D#]before
[C]Him [D7/C]whom [G/B]heav'n [C]and [D]earth adore,
[Bm/F#]So may [Em]we with [C]willing [G]feet
[C]Ever [G/B]seek [Am]Thy [D7]mercy [G]seat.

Verse 3:
[G]As they offered gifts [C/G]most rare
[C/G]At that [G]manger rude and bare,
[Em]So may we [Am/E]with [Em]holy [Cm/D#]joy,
[C]Pure, [D7/C]and [G/B]free [C]from [D]sin's alloy,
[Bm/F#]All our costliest [Em]treasures [G]bring,
[C]Christ, [D7/C]to [G/B]Thee [Am]our [D7]heav'nly [G]King.

Verse 4:
[G]Holy Jesus, every day
[C/G]Keep us [G]in the narrow way;
[Em]And, when earthly things [Cm/D#]are past,
[C]Bring [D7/C]our [G/B]ransomed [D]souls at [G]last
[Bm/F#]Where they [Em]need no [C]star [D7]to [G]guide,
[C]Where [D7/C]no [G/B]clouds [Am]Thy [D7]glory [G]hide.
